## Why This Question Is Asked
This question evaluates practical design skills for privacy-aware, scalable data ingestion, testing strategies, and architectural decision-making under regional compliance requirements.

## Key Concepts
- Centralized policy registry with dynamic privacy rule enforcement
- Per-record lineage tracking via unique identifiers
- Iceberg upserts with schema evolution support
- Regional isolation and late-data handling (up to 60 minutes)
- Privacy conformance tests and data-quality validation gates

## Code Example
```javascript
// Policy application sketch
function applyPolicy(record, policyRegistry) {
  const policies = policyRegistry.getPolicies(record.region, record.dataType);
  return policies.reduce((r, policy) => policy.transform(r), record);
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
This question evaluates your ability to design scalable, multi-tenant data pipelines that handle schema diversity, guarantee data quality, and maintain operational reliability under high throughput.

## Key Concepts
- Per-tenant schema registry and validation
- Idempotent upserts using Iceberg MERGE operations
- Late data handling with time-partitioned snapshots
- Data quality enforcement via JSON Schema and Great Expectations
- Observability through comprehensive monitoring and automated rollback testing

## Code Example
```javascript
function upsertEvent(table, event) {
  // Validate against tenant-specific schema
  const isValid = validateEvent(event.tenant_id, event);
  if (!isValid) throw new Error('Schema validation failed');

  // Perform idempotent upsert using MERGE
  return table.merge()
    .whenMatched().updateAll()
    .whenNotMatched().insertAll()
    .execute();
}
```
